          "explanation": "<div class=\"ml-en\"><p>$\\hat{p} = \\dfrac{940}{1000} = 0.94$. Under $H_0$ the standard error uses $p_0 = 0.9$: $SE = \\sqrt{\\dfrac{0.9 \\times 0.1}{1000}} = \\sqrt{0.00009} = 0.009487$. Then $z_0 = \\dfrac{0.94 - 0.90}{0.009487} = \\dfrac{0.04}{0.009487} = 4.22$. It is POSITIVE because $\\hat{p} > p_0$. Using $\\hat{p}$ in the standard error instead of $p_0$ would give about 5.3, and 6.32 comes from omitting the $p(1-p)$ factor.</p></div><div class=\"ml-vi\"><p>$\\hat{p} = \\dfrac{940}{1000} = 0.94$. Dưới $H_0$, sai số chuẩn dùng $p_0 = 0.9$: $SE = \\sqrt{\\dfrac{0.9 \\times 0.1}{1000}} = \\sqrt{0.00009} = 0.009487$. Khi đó $z_0 = \\dfrac{0.94 - 0.90}{0.009487} = \\dfrac{0.04}{0.009487} = 4.22$. Giá trị DƯƠNG vì $\\hat{p} > p_0$. Nếu dùng $\\hat{p}$ trong sai số chuẩn thay vì $p_0$ sẽ ra khoảng 5.3, còn 6.32 đến từ việc bỏ thừa số $p(1-p)$.</p></div>"
